  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Civic Role
    
    Zhachelang zhihi'Opalum serves as Organizer-of-Record for the Tide Custom, the Aurora Stack festival of public prosperity-displays through which wealth is transmuted into political legitimacy. She coordinates the display of relics, the sequencing of ceremonies, and — a detail seldom noted — the careful spatial separation between surface-dwellers and those who attend from the deep tunnels. An earlier archive designates her simply as "festival herald"; the elevation to Organizer-of-Record appears to have followed her involvement in the Abyss Collapse Tide emergency (see below), though no formal appointment record survives in the ice I have access to.
    
    She is a member of the Holdborn (ice-thresh) faction and a resident of both Aurora Stack and Thrall☽ Vavmastius, the volcanic settlement where the Communion cult took root. Her robes — white silk, silver threading, aurora-glass clasps — are noted in every account. The consistency of the description suggests either a uniform or a deliberate self-presentation. I incline toward the latter.
    
    ## Affiliations and the Question of Belief
    
    Zhachelang was present when the Communion, the Nightshelf cult sworn to deep-communion through blood-rite, first formed near Thrall☽ Vavmastius. She is listed as a believer of Pactum∴myster, the Communion's doctrine of silence-bound power, and she never ceased attending its gatherings. She is also recorded as a practitioner of ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, the Nightshelf memory-fracturing technique discovered by Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss — a dangerous discipline whose practitioners rarely emerge unchanged.
    
    She carries a pouch of fire-core ash patterned in ☽'visois' Mask configurations predating guilds and councils, alongside crystal fragments that refract light in colors that, by multiple accounts, should not exist. She denies owning the pouch. No one presses her. The ice recorded her presence at the announcement of the artifact known as Dagger Vaesacsorius and marks her as a survivor of whatever attended that event — the phrasing in the original chronicle is carefully imprecise.
    
    Accounts describe her as once possessing genuine warmth. Something has shifted. The precision she brings to her duties reads less like competence than containment.
    
    ## The Abyss Collapse Tide and ☽'Naevaeum~
    
    During the Abyss Collapse Tide, Zhachelang coordinated emergency fire-core redistribution under Flipper Accord provision. She carried supplies into the deep tunnels where Magister ☽'Naevaeum~ Depth-walker, a Nightshelf hermit, had spent three days sealing thermal fissures without rest. Zhachelang stayed to help. Both emerged bearing matching cold-burn discoloration — frost-patterned marks on their left flippers that no medical account adequately explains.
    
    Zhachelang now experiences whisper-echoes during ceremonies, the same perceptual corruption through which ☽'Naevaeum~ communes with the deep. She dismisses this when asked.
    
    What began as Accord-sanctioned inventory audits became regular contact, then something neither party names in any surviving record. Through the courier Splitpath, Zhachelang sent aurora-crystals charged under specific light; ☽'Naevaeum~ answered with unmarked fire-cores left warm. When ☽'Naevaeum~ sealed access to their ledge during the Long Dark, Zhachelang broke through the barrier, losing an aurora-glass clasp to the rough stone. She did not stop to collect it.
    
    ## The Succession Crisis
    
    When the death of Luminary Meridian-of-the-First-Light left Aurora Stack without settled authority, Zhachelang invoked Accord civic provision to postpone the Tide Custom, citing fire-core allocations she had no authorization to guarantee. It was the act of a last functioning civic officer treating procedure as though it still carried weight — which, in the absence of anyone with better standing, it did.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771576958332_0", anchor: "She is a member of the Holdborn (ice-thresh) faction and a resident of both Aurora Stack and Thrall☽ Vavmastius", text: "An Aurora Stack merchant. Holdborn faction. Communion cult member. Pactum∴myster adherent — the doctrine that punishes you for speaking its tenets. Crystalline Spiral practitioner — the discipline I have already noted devours its users' memories. Resident of both the sunlit spires and the volcanic settlement. How extraordinary that no one in any faction apparently paused to observe that this penguin was simultaneously enrolled in every contradictory allegiance the Berg offers. Either she is the most accomplished compartmentalizer alive or every organization she belongs to has stopped checking its rolls. Both possibilities are fascinating.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576958332_1", anchor: "citing fire-core allocations she had no authorization to guarantee", text: "She may have had more authorization than I credited her. The Flipper Accord was renegotiated three times in secret before the public version was signed — I found the drafts in administrative ice so deep it had turned cobalt. The second draft contains an emergency redistribution clause granting civic officers provisional allocation authority during succession gaps. This clause does not appear in the ratified text. Either Zhachelang had access to a draft no one else remembers, or she invented a provision and no one was positioned to contradict her. The result was identical.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576958332_2", anchor: "crystal fragments that refract light in colors that, by multiple accounts, should not exist", text: "Three sources. Unconnected. Describing the same impossible colors independently. I would very much like to dismiss this.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
